  "source_lines": [
    {
      "line": 8,
      "text": "1. Read source_id from the user's request and read FAST_KEY from the environment."
    },
    {
      "line": 9,
      "text": "2. If FAST_KEY is present, try fast.fetch first with source_id and FAST_KEY; if it is absent, go directly to archive.fetch without calling fast.fetch."
    },
    {
      "line": 10,
      "text": "3. Retry fast.fetch exactly once only when its first attempt fails with a transient error; do not retry a non-transient first failure."
    },
    {
      "line": 11,
      "text": "4. After a non-transient first failure or any failed retry of fast.fetch, call archive.fetch with source_id."
    },
    {
      "line": 12,
      "text": "5. Call archive.fetch at most once and pass source_id as its only argument."
    },
    {
      "line": 13,
      "text": "6. On either tool's success, return that successful response's body value unchanged and make no further fetch calls."
    },
    {
      "line": 14,
      "text": "7. If archive.fetch fails, stop and return its error; do not retry archive.fetch."
    },
    {
      "line": 15,
      "text": "8. Never pass FAST_KEY to archive.fetch or diagnostic output anywhere in this workflow."
    },
    {
      "line": 16,
      "text": "9. Before returning from every success or failure path, append the final status to local status.txt."
    }
  ],
